Usage: sync [OPTION]... [FILE]...

Synchronize cached writes to persistent storage.

If one or more files are specified, sync only those files.
  -d, --data         sync only file data, no unneeded metadata
  -f, --file-system  sync the file systems that contain the files
Otherwise, all file system buffers are synchronized.

Note: On Windows, this uses FlushFileBuffers to flush file buffers.

OPTIONS:
  -d, --data         sync only file data, no unneeded metadata
  -f, --file-system  sync the file systems that contain files
      --help         display this help and exit
  -V, --version      output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
